From 363370bdb3e87ca966224dfb08a3b5a56eaf29f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orlfman <25542856+orlfman@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:57:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] linux: add Intel CPU package power meter

Add IntelCPUPower ("CPU:61.3W limit:250W"): the CPU package power from
the Intel RAPL powercap energy counters, against the long term (PL1)
limit, as a bar by default. Power is the energy used since the previous
refresh divided by the time in between, so the first refresh has none;
counter wrap-around at max_energy_range_uj is accounted for. All
intel-rapl:N package zones are summed; their subzones and the
intel-rapl-mmio copies of the same counters are skipped.

The counters are root-only unless the system makes them readable; the
meter then shows "no access" instead of "N/A". Like the AMD GPU sampler,
the counters are looked for again while missing and after they
disappear, the limits are retried until they read, and the counters are
read at most once per refresh. INTELRAPL_SYSFS_ROOT allows pointing the
sampler at a fake sysfs tree for testing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
